---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Data Retention Policy" description="Data Retention Policy of New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG.">
    
    <section class="bg-linear-to-b from-teal-950/40 via-background to-background pt-20 pb-12 text-center relative border-b border-border/40">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary tracking-wider uppercase mb-2 block">🗂️ Data Lifecycle Management</span>
            <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground mb-4">Data Retention Policy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
                Guidelines on how long New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG retains personal data in compliance with GDPR.
            </p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-muted-foreground/60 mt-3 font-medium">Last updated: May 27, 2026</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground space-y-6">
            
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">1. Introduction & Principles</h2>
            <p>
                <strong>New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG</strong> ("we", "us", "our") is committed to retaining personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected. This policy complies with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the Irish Data Protection Acts 1988–2018.
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Data is kept only to satisfy operational, legal, contractual, or legitimate business needs.</li>
                <li>Records are reviewed regularly and deleted securely when no longer required.</li>
                <li>Fully anonymised data used for statistics and reporting may be retained indefinitely.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">2. Specific Retention Periods</h2>
            <p>We apply the following retention timeframes to different categories of personal data:</p>
            
            <div class="space-y-4 border-l-2 border-primary/30 pl-4 my-4">
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">✉️ General Inquiries</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>1 year</strong> from the date of submission (Legitimate interest — to maintain correspondence history).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">🎟️ Event Registrations</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>2 years</strong> from the date of the event (Contractual necessity — for administration and follow-up loops).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">🎓 Leadership Programme Records</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>5 years</strong> from programme completion (Legitimate interest — for alumni engagement and certificates).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">🌿 Branch Applications (Active Leaders)</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>Duration of branch activity + 3 years</strong> (Contractual necessity & legal obligation to manage branch relations).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">❌ Branch Applications (Unsuccessful / Withdrawn)</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>1 year</strong> from the date of the application decision (Legitimate interest — to manage processed records).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">📊 Grant Services & Consulting Clients</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>7 years</strong> from the date of the last service (Contractual necessity — for mandatory reporting and audit purposes).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">💰 Financial & Transaction Records</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>7 years</strong> from the date of transaction (Legal obligation — to comply with Irish tax legislation under the Taxes Consolidation Act 1997).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">📈 Marketing Communications (Brevo Newsletters)</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>Until consent is withdrawn</strong> or after <strong>3 years of total inactivity</strong> (Consent-based infrastructure).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">🌐 Website Analytics (Google Analytics)</p>
                    <p class="text-sm"><strong>26 months</strong> from the date of collection (Legitimate interest — to monitor performance and safety).</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">3. Secure Deletion Procedures</h2>
            <p>Once a retention period expires, data is destroyed using secure industry standards:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Digital Records:</strong> Permanently purged from active databases and third-party subprocessors (Brevo, Cloudflare) within 30 days. Regular backup overwrites occur automatically.</li>
                <li><strong>Physical Documents:</strong> Any printed paper records containing sensitive personal data are securely shredded.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">4. Extended Retention & Exceptions</h2>
            <p>Data may be held longer only under exceptional circumstances: where required by Irish law, during ongoing legal disputes or investigations, or under official regulatory holds.</p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">5. Your Rights & Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Under the GDPR, you have the "right to be forgotten" and can request the early erasure of your personal data. We will comply unless a conflicting legal obligation (such as revenue compliance) requires us to hold it. 
            </p>
            <p>
                To request data deletion or access, please email us at <a href="mailto:info@lifeintegration.ie" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">info@lifeintegration.ie</a>. If you are unsatisfied with our response, you have the right to escalate your request to the Data Protection Commission (DPC) at <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">www.dataprotection.ie</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

</Layout>